Z||000005||fropuff||01-11-2001||06:22 PM||||I know you said good paint, but I paid $2200 for mine in April.  It had some okay paint, but it needed some work. (it's those frickin people that think keying is funny)  I paid around $600 for paint.  The rest of it was in GREAT condition.  Had and still has 62K original miles on it.  I guess it comes down who you buy it from.  If they're no expert on Fieros, they think they're worth a fortune becuase they're "rare".  Not too rare.  The guy I bought mine from was somewhat an expert on Fieros, and he was asking $3000, but I talked him down.  I guess if you want one in great condition, you should expect around $4000.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||01-11-2001||06:37 PM||||I gave about 2000.00 for mine when it had 74,000 miles.  Ran great looked nice inside and out.  Shortly after buying it, I did a major brake job, A/C replacement that summer(1996), tires, coil, dist. module, etc. etc. etc. exhaust manifold. etc... etc........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I lost track, but I have 4 or 5 thousand dollars worth of " fix me!" receipts in my folder to date. WOOO HOOOO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It's all good.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||6
